## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical, beginner-friendly observability implementation: instrumenting a new service end-to-end with minimal changes and validating traces in a production UI.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry auto-instrumentation
- Trace-context propagation and log correlation
- Lightweight instrumentation for HTTP and database spans
- OTLP exporter configuration and backend dashboard validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Node example: enable auto-instrumentation
// Install: @opentelemetry/api @opentelemetry/sdk-node @opentelemetry/instrumentation-http
import { NodeSDK } from '@opentelemetry/sdk-node';
import { getNodeAutoInstrumentations } from '@opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node';

const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  instrumentations: [getNodeAutoInstrumentations()],
  serviceName: 'accounts-service',
  traceExporter: new OTLPTraceExporter()
});
sdk.start();

// Trace ID in logs
import { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api';
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const traceId = trace.getActiveSpan()?.spanContext().traceId;
  console.log(`Request ${req.method} ${req.path} [trace=${traceId}]`);
  next();
});
```

## Validation Plan
- Configure OTLP exporter to your backend (Jaeger/Tempo/Grafana)
- Verify HTTP request spans appear in dashboard
- Confirm database query spans are captured
- Check trace IDs appear in structured logs
- Test end-to-end with synthetic request and validate trace flow

## Why This Is Asked

Telemetry quality is critical for root cause analysis and cross-service tracing; this checks practical skills for CI, instrumentation, and rollback safety.

## Key Concepts

- Telemetry integrity, trace propagation, OpenTelemetry, CI gates, canary deployments
- Error budgets and dashboards alignment
- Synthetic validation and fallback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// OpenTelemetry middleware for trace propagation
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');

function ensureTraceId(req, res, next) {
  const carrier = propagation.createExtractHeadersCarrier(req.headers);
  const ctx = propagation.extract(context.active(), carrier);

  if (!trace.getSpan(ctx).spanContext().traceId) {
    const tracer = trace.getTracer('default');
    const span = tracer.startSpan('fallback-trace');
    propagation.inject(context.active(), carrier);
  }
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure telemetry coverage and what would trigger a rollback?
- What trade-offs exist when dropping events missing trace_id?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical incident response capabilities for multi-region systems experiencing partial service degradation, requiring coordination between observability, gradual deployment, and safe rollback procedures.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped logging and metrics aggregation
- Canary deployment strategies in distributed systems
- Queue depth monitoring and database latency optimization
- Progressive traffic splitting and validation workflows
- Automated rollback with metric-driven decision points

## Code Example
